Receipts: `mcp__pm_execution__python_execute`, sandbox `/work`, exit 0, wall 0.17 s. Scope limits: stdlib-only, single component semantics; does not establish NGFF library behavior or any application behavior.

### W1 — NGFF-style transform composition order (receipt exec-wekc6v6a, `code_sha256 ad3f081e…e96ae23`)
- Code: sequential application of scale/translation lists to x=(3,5); scale=(0.5,2.0), translation=(10,20).
- Expected (from S3): scale-then-translation ≠ translation-then-scale.
- stdout: `scale->translation: [11.5, 30.0]`; `translation->scale: [6.5, 50.0]`; `orders differ: True`.
- Discriminates: whether stored coordinates + calibration reproduce the same physical point after a save/load round trip. Any proposal that stores user-visible coordinates without pinning the applied order fails this check.

### W2 — exact float64 round-trip through JSON (same receipt)
- Code: `json.loads(json.dumps(v)) == v` (plus struct bit compare for the min subnormal) on 0.1, 1e308, min subnormal, max double, π.
- stdout: all `exact: True`; subnormal `bit-exact: True`.
- Supports (component-level, CPython `json` only): storing annotation coordinates as JSON doubles loses no precision. Does NOT generalize to other serializers, NaN handling, or decimal-format consumers; NaN/Inf must be excluded at the schema level (JSON does not define them).

